cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MC++ or PyMC++ in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "MC++: a toolkit for the construction, manipulation and bounding of factorable functions"
abstract: >-
  MC++ represents factorable functions as directed acyclic graphs and propagates
  through them not only numbers and derivatives but sets: interval enclosures,
  McCormick convex/concave relaxations with subgradients, Taylor and Chebyshev
  models with rigorous remainders, spectral and ellipsoidal bounds, polyhedral
  relaxations, and superposition relaxations.  PyMC++ (the module pymcpp)
  exposes the toolkit to Python.
type: software
authors:
